# Testing & Validation

After implementation, verify automatically — do not mark work complete without running checks.

## Run Sequence

1. `npm install` in `client/`, `server/`, `ai-service/` (if changed)
2. Verify dependencies and env vars exist (`.env.example` as reference)
3. Start MongoDB, backend (`server/`), AI service (`ai-service/`), frontend (`client/`)
4. Verify API routes respond; OpenAI/Cloudinary/Maps/Socket.IO integrations work or degrade gracefully
5. `npm run build` in client — fix compile, lint, import errors
6. Retry until successful

## Integration Checklist

- [ ] MongoDB connection
- [ ] Issue CRUD + complaint ID generation
- [ ] AI classification (or fallback)
- [ ] Cloudinary image upload
- [ ] Maps geolocation/pins
- [ ] Socket.IO real-time events
- [ ] Admin JWT login + protected routes

## Error Policy

Fix compile errors, lint errors, runtime errors, broken routes, missing dependencies, and major console/API failures before stopping. Preserve existing APIs — improve UI without breaking business logic.

## URLs to Report on Completion

Frontend URL, backend URL, admin URL, and any service ports used during verification.
